=== 1. THE MARGIN: can the modulation shut photosynthesis off? ===
  ENSO index over 1948-2024: sd 0.751, max|index| 2.244 (n = 924 months)
  ra_ratio 0.000, npp_leaf_frac 0.600

  hem |      gamma  peak |anom| gross GPP PI |  anom/GPP
   NH |    -0.2457        0.551       38.908 |     1.42 %
   SH |    +1.3583        3.048       21.092 |    14.45 %

  ⇒ worst hemisphere: SH at 14.45 % of its own gross GPP limb.
  STRESS: the gamma multiplier at which the anomaly would reach the limb.
    gamma x 1   ->   14.5 % ok
    gamma x 2   ->   28.9 % ok
    gamma x 4   ->   57.8 % ok
    gamma x 8   ->  115.6 % ⛔ SHUTS PHOTOSYNTHESIS OFF
    gamma x 16  ->  231.2 % ⛔ SHUTS PHOTOSYNTHESIS OFF
  ⇒ it would take a gamma about 7x the fitted one to bite.
  ⚠ CONSERVATIVE AGAINST FERTILISATION (modern npp exceeds npp0) and NOT
    conservative against clearing (luc_scale = 1.1100 in this arm).
  ⚠ ra_ratio is 0 in this arm, so the gross limb IS npp -- the gross
    respiration loop is off by default and adds no headroom here.

