=== 3. WHY: the ENSO index is not zero-mean, and the pools differ ===
  mean ENSO index, whole run 1750-2024 : -0.06098  (sd 0.4092, n 3300)
  mean ENSO index, 1948-2024       : -0.21778  (sd 0.7513, n 924)
  before 1948 the index is identically 0.0, so the two structures are
  bit-identical there and the whole difference is post-1948.

  sustained SH GPP anomaly from the mean: -(+1.3583) x (-0.06098) = +0.08283 GtC/yr
  effective land residence time: veg 8.60 + soil 26.90 = 35.50 yr
  tau_soil_fast (the OLD form's only pool):            2.00 yr
  => extra land stock in the NEW form: +2.7747 GtC = -1.3063 ppm of CO2
  ⚠ THAT IS A FULL-EQUILIBRIUM ESTIMATE and the anomaly has only run since
    1948 (76 yr against a 36 yr time constant), with the ocean and
    CO2 fertilisation both damping it -- so it is an OVERESTIMATE of the
    measured shift, and should be read for its SIGN and ORDER only.

